    "evidence_text": "Skip-Thought  consists of an encoder and two decoders.\n\nInferSent  instead pre-trains the model in a manner of supervised learning.\n\nIt uses a large-scale NLI dataset as the\n\npre-training task to learn the sentence representation.\n\nMethod\tOur method follows the same input format and the model architecture with original BERT.\n\nThe proposed method solely concerns the NSP task.\n\nsuggest the order discrimination is essential for BERT pre-training.\n\nNote that these in-adjacent sentences will introduce much more training noise to the model.\n\nExperiment Settings\tThis section gives detailed experiment settings.\n\nTo accelerate the training speed, two-phase training  is adopted.\n\nWe used a dropout probability of 0.1 on all layers.\n\nWe explore three method settings for comparison.\n\nBERT-PN is used to verify the feasibility of PSP.\n\nThe predictions were obtained by evaluating the training checkpoint with the best validation performance.\n\nThe improvement should be attributed to better semantic representation.\n\nTABREF26.\n\nDRCD  is also a Chinese MRC data set.\n\nThe data follows the format of SQuAD.\n\nFor Chinese NLP tasks, we pre-train the model using Chinese corpus.\n\nNote that the Chinese ERNIE 2.0 is equipped with 5 different",
